As I can read from the spoilers NH3.1 should be around 53 levels deep or
so. This includes the Hack standard 20-25 levels plus the maze levels.
It also includes the NH3.1 special levels like gnomish mines, quest levels
etc etc.

Theese extra levels also means a LOT of running around on levels which are
quite boring. Im for the moment exploring the mazes below The valley of the 
dead (below the castle) and they are boring me stiff. (Just like all theese
mazes in NH2+ (I think they were up to level 60) and NH3.0).
If you are running a caracter in NH3.1 who has taken the castle, then normally
he is so good (thats what I belive anyway) that he wants some action. Not just
the time consuming look for the stairs in the mazes. (Yes I have read a spell
book of magic mapping but I dont want to waste the few spells untill I really
need them)

My suggestion is:

1. Gnomish mines should always be lit (some are) exept perhaps for a few
passages that might be unlit. 
Think of them as real mines with lots of working gnomes. Would they really 
be unlit?? I think not.

2. Mazes are ok as long as they are few. (Two or three would be enough
I think)

3. In those mazes there should sometimes be inscriptions in the floor/walls
that points in the direction of the stairs. Think of it as 'helps' from
other explorers who has already been here.

4. Perhaps another 'tool' could be added. A thread roll (sp?. Thin string)
so that if you use it, the maze should be 'lit up' were you walk around.
Perhaps a better way is that you find pieces of the thread close to the
stairs??? Who of you would enter caves or mazes WITHOUT a thread roll in
thees days by the way? Not me.

The reason for my disliking is really that the game 'slows up' in theese
parts (read exitement slows up). Add a few teasers to them to make them
more thrilling or remove them totally. (Im not sure I want to make the
game smaller, but rather increase the action. This is in line with the
D-team's tries to increase the challenge for us, with all theese new and
exiting spec-levels.)

Hope that You and the D-team agrees.

